From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Tom Englund <tomenglund26@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 26 Oct 2026 09:58:32 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] nvidia: take the API lock for read for GET_SURFACE_INFO

NV0041_CTRL_CMD_GET_SURFACE_INFO is flagged without
RMCTRL_FLAGS_API_LOCK_READONLY, so it takes the global RM API lock for
write. nvidia-modeset calls it while registering every framebuffer
(DRM ADDFB2), and a write acquire waits for every READ-locked control
of every other client: when an app starts, the compositor's main thread
waited 2.9 ms behind the app's PERF_BOOST GSP RPC.

The control only reads the Memory object's descriptor (size, address
space, physical attributes, compression coverage) and HW resource
attributes, which are fixed once the memory is allocated. Frees, allocs,
dups and maps take the API lock for write, and the control still takes
its client lock for write and the GPU lock, so a READ API lock is
enough.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 src/nvidia/src/kernel/rmapi/control.c | 16 ++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 16 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/nvidia/src/kernel/rmapi/control.c b/src/nvidia/src/kernel/rmapi/control.c
index faa75611..2305cded 100644
--- a/src/nvidia/src/kernel/rmapi/control.c
+++ b/src/nvidia/src/kernel/rmapi/control.c
@@ -42,6 +42,7 @@
 #include "ctrl/ctrl0000/ctrl0000gpuacct.h" // NV0000_CTRL_CMD_GPUACCT_*
 #include "ctrl/ctrl2080/ctrl2080tmr.h" // NV2080_CTRL_CMD_TIMER_SCHEDULE
 #include "ctrl/ctrl2080/ctrl2080fb.h" // NV2080_CTRL_CMD_FB_GET_MEM_ALIGNMENT
+#include "ctrl/ctrl0041.h" // NV0041_CTRL_CMD_GET_SURFACE_INFO
 
 static NV_STATUS
 releaseDeferRmCtrlBuffer(RmCtrlDeferredCmd* pRmCtrlDeferredCmd)
@@ -960,6 +961,21 @@ serverControlLookupLockFlags
             *pAccess = LOCK_ACCESS_READ;
         }
 
+        //
+        // GET_SURFACE_INFO only reads the Memory object's descriptor and HW
+        // resource attributes, which are fixed once the memory is allocated.
+        // Frees, allocs, dups and maps take the API lock for write, and the
+        // control still takes the client lock (write) and the GPU lock, so
+        // a READ API lock is enough. nvidia-modeset calls it while registering
+        // every framebuffer; with the WRITE lock that waited for every other
+        // client's READ-locked control (e.g. a PERF_BOOST GSP RPC when an app
+        // starts), stalling the compositor.
+        //
+        if (pRmCtrlParams->cmd == NV0041_CTRL_CMD_GET_SURFACE_INFO)
+        {
+            *pAccess = LOCK_ACCESS_READ;
+        }
+
         //
         // ROUTE_TO_PHYSICAL controls always take the READ API lock. This only applies
         // to GSP clients: Only there can we guarantee per-gpu execution of commands.
